WEBVTT

00:07.632 --> 00:09.634
[theme music playing]

00:29.112 --> 00:30.363
[line ringing]

00:41.082 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

00:47.046 --> 00:48.214
[elevator dings]

00:49.090 --> 00:50.717
[indistinct chatter]

00:53.887 --> 00:55.889
[suspenseful music playing]

00:57.724 --> 01:00.727
[Hee-joo] I can't do this.
Just let me out.

01:00.810 --> 01:03.980
- [officer 2] We're on the road right now.
- It'll be okay if you just let me out.

01:04.064 --> 01:07.484
It'll be okay, so let me out!

01:07.567 --> 01:08.735
[Hee-joo gasping for air]

01:21.790 --> 01:22.791
[Yeon-hui] I don't care.

01:24.209 --> 01:28.004
Anyway, now that he's been moved,
I don't need to pay anymore, right?

01:29.756 --> 01:30.840
[door opens]

01:31.841 --> 01:33.885
[gasps] Hey, Sa-eon.

01:34.469 --> 01:35.345
[exhales]

01:35.887 --> 01:37.013
When did you get here?

01:38.681 --> 01:40.141
[Sa-eon] Let's go in.

01:40.225 --> 01:42.101
Oh my. You really are polite.

01:45.772 --> 01:47.398
I'm curious about something.

01:47.482 --> 01:48.316
[Yeon-hui] What?

01:49.400 --> 01:52.695
Why won't Hee-joo speak?

01:52.779 --> 01:55.240
What do you mean? Don't you know?

01:55.323 --> 01:58.993
She's in shock
from a car accident as a child.

01:59.994 --> 02:01.162
That shock…

02:03.164 --> 02:04.457
affects her to this day?

02:07.794 --> 02:09.337
Selective mutism

02:09.420 --> 02:12.382
is when someone stops speaking
due to psychological factors.

02:12.465 --> 02:16.511
Isn't it strange that she's been like that
for over 20 years?

02:17.095 --> 02:19.097
Well, the guilt was just so overwhelming.

02:19.180 --> 02:20.265
What guilt?

02:21.349 --> 02:24.310
Was the car accident Hee-joo's fault?

02:24.894 --> 02:27.856
She lost her brother,
and her sister went deaf.

02:27.939 --> 02:30.942
How could she be okay after that?
She shouldn't be.

02:33.111 --> 02:33.945
[sighs]

02:34.028 --> 02:34.863
But…

02:35.613 --> 02:37.157
why do you ask that?

02:38.116 --> 02:40.451
It seems you keep forgetting.

02:41.619 --> 02:42.996
Hee-joo's my wife.

02:43.580 --> 02:46.875
Please be careful how you treat her.
Watch what you say and do.

02:50.795 --> 02:51.754
[music ends]

02:56.050 --> 02:56.885
What was that?

02:57.719 --> 02:59.721
Is he looking out for Hee-joo?

02:59.804 --> 03:02.056
[classical music playing]

03:04.475 --> 03:05.602
Sa-eon.

03:05.685 --> 03:07.270
It's been a while.

03:07.353 --> 03:09.898
I almost forgot your face.
Let's meet up more often.

03:09.981 --> 03:11.941
Yeah, you're much more handsome now.

03:12.025 --> 03:15.111
- In-a must be treating you well.
- [woman 1] Yeah.

03:15.194 --> 03:16.446
- [woman 2] Let's toast.
- Cheers.

03:16.529 --> 03:17.780
- Cheers.
- Let's toast.

03:24.495 --> 03:25.830
[woman 3] It's nice.

03:27.081 --> 03:29.626
- [woman 2] I can taste apples.
- [woman 3] They're well-prepared.

03:29.709 --> 03:32.712
- [woman 2] Such a sommelier.
- [woman 1] That's right.

03:38.885 --> 03:39.802
Spokesperson.

03:41.888 --> 03:42.847
Sir.

03:42.931 --> 03:46.100
When do you plan on joining your father?

03:46.184 --> 03:47.018
[sighs]

03:47.977 --> 03:50.521
I guess you haven't received
a satisfactory offer yet.

03:50.605 --> 03:53.816
Things should be clear-cut
between parents and children as well.

03:55.860 --> 03:57.070
[phone vibrating]

03:58.029 --> 03:59.030
Excuse me.

04:00.990 --> 04:02.992
[intriguing music playing]

04:05.828 --> 04:06.871
[Sa-eon] What did you say?

04:07.664 --> 04:08.790
Supplementary pages?

04:09.290 --> 04:10.124
[scoffs]

04:10.833 --> 04:12.543
If you don't know, listen carefully, 406.

04:12.627 --> 04:14.963
Hee-joo isn't supplementary pages.

04:15.046 --> 04:16.881
She's a brand-new language.

04:17.966 --> 04:22.345
She's repeated the same hand movements
thousands of times to become who she is.

04:23.054 --> 04:24.430
People don't know that.

04:24.514 --> 04:27.934
So don't talk about my wife like that.

04:33.564 --> 04:35.900
Excuse me, where did you find that?

04:36.693 --> 04:37.527
Oh.

04:38.194 --> 04:39.988
In the bathroom.

04:47.620 --> 04:50.873
You say you know her so well.
Then why did you do that?

04:52.208 --> 04:55.336
Why did you tell her
not to think you were a couple?

04:55.420 --> 04:56.462
[elevator dings]

04:59.590 --> 05:01.592
[intriguing music continues playing]

05:09.392 --> 05:10.560
[gasps]

05:18.568 --> 05:20.236
[dramatic music playing]

05:34.250 --> 05:35.251
[thuds]

05:38.212 --> 05:39.213
[music ends]

05:40.131 --> 05:41.007
Are you okay?

05:52.060 --> 05:52.977
[Sa-eon sighs]

06:00.777 --> 06:02.445
Why were you on the railing?

06:02.528 --> 06:04.655
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

06:04.739 --> 06:05.573
[hiccups]

06:07.617 --> 06:09.619
[gripping music playing]

06:19.504 --> 06:20.838
[Sa-eon] Were you on a call?

06:21.422 --> 06:22.340
[scoffs]

06:24.550 --> 06:25.635
Hong Hee-joo…

06:27.470 --> 06:29.055
can't make calls.

06:36.020 --> 06:38.147
Why were you on the phone?

06:42.693 --> 06:44.862
[mouthing]

06:44.946 --> 06:46.072
Make a sound.

06:48.074 --> 06:50.576
Make a sound like you just did.
Hiccup or whatever.

06:53.037 --> 06:53.871
Should I force you?

07:05.633 --> 07:06.676
[scoffs]

07:08.553 --> 07:09.637
Hong Hee-joo.

07:11.806 --> 07:13.182
How could you?

07:14.142 --> 07:15.143
[music ends]

07:15.226 --> 07:16.394
[phone vibrating]

07:31.284 --> 07:32.493
Go ahead.

07:38.916 --> 07:40.543
[phone vibrating]

07:44.213 --> 07:45.131
Yes?

07:45.214 --> 07:47.133
[Do-jae] The call went over
the ten-minute mark.

07:47.216 --> 07:48.217
We got the location.

07:48.301 --> 07:49.510
Where is it?

07:49.594 --> 07:50.845
[Do-jae] Don't be surprised.

07:50.928 --> 07:53.639
Sogong-dong.
The hotel you're at right now.

07:54.223 --> 07:57.143
I think this person is much closer to you
than we thought.

07:57.977 --> 08:00.229
Is there anyone suspicious around you?

08:01.105 --> 08:03.107
[suspenseful music playing]

08:06.611 --> 08:07.445
[scoffs]

08:08.488 --> 08:10.072
What am I thinking?

08:12.283 --> 08:13.201
Wait.

08:14.702 --> 08:16.621
Are you saying he's here right now?

08:16.704 --> 08:17.830
[elevator dings]

08:28.382 --> 08:29.800
[breathing heavily]

08:34.889 --> 08:35.848
[elevator dings]

08:37.892 --> 08:39.393
[suspenseful music continues playing]

08:59.664 --> 09:00.790
[music ends]

09:01.707 --> 09:04.168
Why aren't you going in?

09:19.433 --> 09:21.435
[slow music playing]

09:31.404 --> 09:32.947
[Jang-ho] Kyu-jin.

09:33.030 --> 09:34.615
There must not be

09:35.324 --> 09:38.744
even a single rusty spoon in my household.

09:40.788 --> 09:43.124
Think carefully
which is more important to you.

09:44.292 --> 09:47.378
Being a mother to your son

09:47.461 --> 09:50.256
or maintaining your status
as my daughter-in-law?

10:09.859 --> 10:11.694
[tense music playing]

10:16.907 --> 10:17.992
[Sa-eon sighs]

10:18.618 --> 10:20.369
[panting]

10:23.539 --> 10:24.540
[line ringing]

10:25.499 --> 10:27.209
- [exhales heavily]
- [Do-jae] Yes, Mr. Paik.

10:27.293 --> 10:29.128
Secure the guest list.

10:29.211 --> 10:32.465
Hurry up and work on removing
the voice modulation too.

10:32.548 --> 10:34.383
EPISODE 5

10:34.467 --> 10:35.676
[door closes]

10:41.140 --> 10:42.308
[Sa-eon] Hong Hee-joo.

10:49.023 --> 10:51.609
Do you still have that scar?

10:56.614 --> 10:58.240
[mellow music playing]

11:02.286 --> 11:03.287
When you were a kid,

11:04.163 --> 11:05.748
you almost got bitten by a big dog.

11:07.249 --> 11:10.211
Even back then,
you didn't let out a single scream.

11:11.545 --> 11:13.798
How could such a young girl

11:14.715 --> 11:16.592
hold back a scream?

11:23.516 --> 11:25.351
You're incredible, Hee-joo.

11:26.227 --> 11:28.437
I wonder how long
you'll be able to hold out.

11:29.647 --> 11:30.564
I'm curious.

11:37.321 --> 11:39.073
[door opens, closes]

11:42.034 --> 11:43.619
[young Hee-joo] "Our next story."

11:43.702 --> 11:46.288
"Pope Benedict XVI resigned,

11:46.372 --> 11:48.666
and Pope Francis was elected."

11:48.749 --> 11:51.544
"This is the first papal resignation
in 600 years

11:51.627 --> 11:52.920
while the pope is still alive."

11:53.003 --> 11:54.171
[Yeon-hui] Hee-joo!

11:59.468 --> 12:00.970
What's this?

12:01.053 --> 12:03.931
Your dream is to be a newscaster?
A newscaster?

12:04.557 --> 12:07.560
How can you be a newscaster?
You can't even speak! How?

12:10.521 --> 12:12.690
[voice shaking] Didn't I
make myself clear?

12:13.399 --> 12:15.901
The moment you start chattering
in front of In-a,

12:16.610 --> 12:19.405
you and I will be kicked out
of this house.

12:19.488 --> 12:21.157
[Yeon-hui exhales frustratingly]

12:21.240 --> 12:23.242
[dramatic music playing]

12:28.581 --> 12:30.124
[sobbing]

12:36.672 --> 12:38.507
[dog growling]

12:39.383 --> 12:40.342
[barks]

12:40.926 --> 12:42.011
[breathing heavily]

12:43.804 --> 12:44.930
[barks]

12:45.723 --> 12:47.141
[dog growling]

12:49.143 --> 12:50.603
[dog barking]

12:51.687 --> 12:52.688
[music stops]

12:52.771 --> 12:54.398
- [thuds]
- [dog whimpering]

13:00.404 --> 13:02.656
[mellow music playing]

13:16.712 --> 13:18.339
I'm sure it wasn't the dog that hit you.

13:20.382 --> 13:21.467
You should fight back.

13:22.301 --> 13:23.719
Be it your mom, sister, or whoever.

13:25.471 --> 13:27.097
Prepare yourself to fight back.

13:29.517 --> 13:30.476
[sighs]

13:30.559 --> 13:34.730
Whether it's parents or family,
there's always a chance for revenge.

13:51.205 --> 13:52.248
You scraped your knee.

13:52.331 --> 13:54.166
[mellow music continues playing]

14:07.846 --> 14:09.515
PAIK SA-EON

14:16.021 --> 14:19.275
[young Sa-eon] It's red,
like your swollen cheek.

14:30.786 --> 14:32.663
[Sa-eon] Hee-joo
isn't supplementary pages.

14:33.581 --> 14:35.332
She's a brand-new language.

14:51.098 --> 14:52.349
[music ends]

15:00.190 --> 15:01.859
[sighs]

15:13.495 --> 15:14.705
[sighs softly]

15:16.624 --> 15:17.458
Hong Hee-joo.

15:18.083 --> 15:19.501
Come out here.

15:19.585 --> 15:21.587
[dramatic music playing]

15:25.966 --> 15:27.051
All this time,

15:28.260 --> 15:30.763
you've been deceiving me, haven't you?

15:31.847 --> 15:32.848
[Sa-eon scoffs]

15:33.390 --> 15:36.185
Don't look at me like you don't know.
I know everything.

15:36.268 --> 15:37.102
Why?

15:38.187 --> 15:39.772
Why did you go that far?

15:39.855 --> 15:41.982
You've deceived me for 20 years!

15:44.610 --> 15:46.904
You even resorted to doing this, but why?

15:48.614 --> 15:51.659
Yeah, let's just say
you were young back then.

15:51.742 --> 15:52.826
But you…

15:53.661 --> 15:56.664
You're not a kid anymore.
You're a grown-up.

15:57.998 --> 16:00.417
At least once you started living with me,

16:01.126 --> 16:03.128
there was no reason to hide it.

16:03.212 --> 16:05.297
[dramatic music continues playing]

16:09.593 --> 16:10.427
[scoffs]

16:19.061 --> 16:20.896
Everyone has secrets.

16:26.402 --> 16:29.488
Don't you have any?
Something you're hiding from me.

16:32.992 --> 16:33.909
[scoffs]

16:39.415 --> 16:40.374
[scoffs]

16:40.457 --> 16:41.458
[music stops]

16:50.801 --> 16:52.261
[slow music playing]

17:03.897 --> 17:06.525
Finalists for the sign language
interpreter interview

17:06.608 --> 17:08.527
will be contacted individually.

17:08.610 --> 17:11.572
They'll start work at the office tomorrow.

17:11.655 --> 17:13.866
The main media reactions
to the hiring are…

17:14.366 --> 17:15.451
[quirky music playing]

17:17.244 --> 17:18.203
[gulps]

17:19.288 --> 17:21.415
"Everyone now has acquired
the right to watch

17:21.498 --> 17:23.500
the president's speech
without discrimination."

17:23.584 --> 17:25.961
"Korean Sign Language is on par
with the Korean language,

17:26.045 --> 17:27.880
ensuring information access for the Deaf…"

17:27.963 --> 17:29.840
- Excuse me, sir?
- [music ends]

17:29.923 --> 17:31.633
Yes, well…

17:31.717 --> 17:34.219
I know I'm lacking. I do, but still…

17:34.303 --> 17:36.096
I worked hard to prepare this.

17:36.180 --> 17:41.185
If something is making you uncomfortable
or making you unhappy, please…

17:43.729 --> 17:44.980
No. [clears throat]

17:46.607 --> 17:48.442
I'm pleased with it.

17:50.194 --> 17:51.445
Great work.

17:55.449 --> 17:57.034
Let's take a quick break.

17:59.036 --> 18:00.329
[amusing music playing]

18:00.412 --> 18:02.164
MEN'S RESTROOM

18:03.540 --> 18:06.794
[Young-woo] My liver enzyme levels
didn't just go up for no reason.

18:06.877 --> 18:09.713
When you get anxious, your liver shrinks.

18:11.590 --> 18:15.469
What? Because of smoking and drinking?
No, that's a misconception.

18:15.552 --> 18:18.889
Accumulated fatigue and stress
are all causes too, you know?

18:20.099 --> 18:22.476
Okay, honey.

18:22.559 --> 18:25.312
Yeah, I'll make sure
to take my supplements.

18:25.395 --> 18:26.563
One more thing.

18:27.189 --> 18:30.692
I'm going to stand tall,
and I'm not going to…

18:32.194 --> 18:33.028
Sir…

18:34.154 --> 18:35.989
- Mr. Paik?
- Mr. Kang?

18:36.073 --> 18:37.616
Yes, sir.

18:38.534 --> 18:39.451
Let's have a word.

18:45.541 --> 18:47.292
[Sa-eon] Mr. Kang, do you…

18:48.377 --> 18:49.962
tell your wife everything?

18:51.296 --> 18:52.798
About that.

18:52.881 --> 18:55.467
I definitely wasn't talking about you.

18:55.551 --> 18:57.594
- It was about my health.
- [Sa-eon] Are there…

18:58.387 --> 18:59.429
no secrets?

18:59.513 --> 19:00.514
Excuse me?

19:00.597 --> 19:01.932
In your marriage,

19:03.517 --> 19:05.769
do you hide anything

19:06.520 --> 19:08.147
or deceive each other?

19:08.230 --> 19:11.817
[spluttering] I don't know. Not really.

19:12.860 --> 19:13.944
Why do you ask?

19:17.030 --> 19:20.284
Is your wife secretly hiding…

19:22.703 --> 19:24.413
emergency funds from you?

19:24.496 --> 19:26.540
[amusing music playing]

19:26.623 --> 19:27.457
No.

19:27.541 --> 19:29.543
What a relief.

19:29.626 --> 19:32.880
As long as it's not about money,
right? [chuckles]

19:33.755 --> 19:35.465
- Is that so?
- Of course.

19:37.801 --> 19:39.428
Also… [clears throat]

19:40.137 --> 19:43.849
sometimes it's necessary to pretend
not to know and let things slide.

19:43.932 --> 19:46.602
That's how you get some breathing room.

19:47.394 --> 19:50.397
It'll be suffocating if you nitpick
and criticize every little thing.

19:52.649 --> 19:53.483
Of course,

19:54.818 --> 19:56.612
that won't be easy,
given your personality.

19:56.695 --> 19:58.113
What's wrong with it?

19:59.781 --> 20:02.242
Like, you're the type
who strives for perfection.

20:04.786 --> 20:08.790
But still, marriage takes effort,
don't you think?

20:09.416 --> 20:11.126
You could try calming your temper.

20:12.002 --> 20:12.836
Effort?

20:17.466 --> 20:19.343
[clock ticking]

20:25.849 --> 20:27.184
[phone vibrates]

20:27.768 --> 20:29.770
[gentle music playing]

20:49.998 --> 20:51.166
What? Goodness!

20:51.250 --> 20:52.960
She passed! She passed!

20:53.543 --> 20:55.879
- She passed!
- [overlapping chatter]

20:55.963 --> 20:56.838
Congratulations.

20:56.922 --> 20:58.465
Congratulations!

20:59.466 --> 21:00.384
She passed!

21:07.432 --> 21:08.433
[music pauses]

21:08.517 --> 21:10.644
CONGRATULATIONS ON PASSING
THE FINAL INTERVIEW.

21:10.727 --> 21:12.145
[Jin-e] You worked hard.

21:12.229 --> 21:14.273
[music continues playing]

21:14.356 --> 21:15.440
Great job.

21:17.734 --> 21:20.445
Go and tell your family the good news.

21:21.405 --> 21:24.199
Should we get some drinks?
What should we get?

21:24.283 --> 21:25.284
- Yeah.
- [Jin-e] Let's go.

21:27.536 --> 21:29.454
- [man] Are you buying?
- [Jin-e] Let's have cake.

21:29.538 --> 21:30.372
[woman] Cake!

21:30.455 --> 21:31.665
[man] It's been so long.

21:42.217 --> 21:43.802
DAD

21:50.392 --> 21:52.519
[gentle music continues playing]

21:54.855 --> 21:57.649
PAIK SA-EON

22:07.159 --> 22:08.243
[Hee-joo] I passed.

22:19.004 --> 22:20.922
There was no special treatment, right?

22:21.006 --> 22:22.841
Did I earn this on my own?

22:27.846 --> 22:28.680
[sighs]

22:29.473 --> 22:31.308
Why is this so hard?

22:46.031 --> 22:47.616
What do I do?

22:47.699 --> 22:48.867
[music ends]

22:48.950 --> 22:49.993
[Young-woo] Almost forgot.

22:50.077 --> 22:52.579
We have a welcome dinner
for the interpreters tomorrow.

22:52.662 --> 22:53.914
We anticipate your attendance.

22:54.748 --> 22:57.918
Normally, holding a company retreat
would be the proper thing to do.

22:58.668 --> 23:01.129
However, many are exhausted
from the workload.

23:01.213 --> 23:03.965
Especially since Mr. Paik
has such a tight schedule,

23:04.049 --> 23:06.051
we'll have a dinner instead.

23:06.760 --> 23:08.053
[amusing music playing]

23:11.848 --> 23:13.350
Sir?

23:14.643 --> 23:16.478
What did you just say?

23:17.395 --> 23:18.480
A company retreat?

23:18.563 --> 23:22.442
No, no. Since you have a busy schedule,
we'll have a dinner…

23:22.526 --> 23:25.654
Aren't they the first sign language
interpreters in the president's office?

23:25.737 --> 23:27.239
The media is interested as well.

23:27.322 --> 23:30.075
Shouldn't we take a commemorative photo
for the press release?

23:31.827 --> 23:33.537
Let's go on a retreat.

23:33.620 --> 23:36.123
How's the weekend for everyone?

23:37.124 --> 23:38.083
I'm free.

23:38.166 --> 23:39.292
[Sa-eon] Sounds good.

23:39.376 --> 23:41.878
Since we're going,
let's make it an overnight trip.

23:41.962 --> 23:43.171
Please arrange the venue.

23:49.511 --> 23:53.140
[employee 1] Wow,
I completely misjudged Mr. Park.

23:54.057 --> 23:55.350
"I'm free."

23:55.433 --> 23:57.853
[employee 2] They call him
Mr. Paik's mini-me for a reason.

23:57.936 --> 24:01.106
No wonder Mr. Paik brought him in
when he started here.

24:01.189 --> 24:02.190
[sighs]

24:02.983 --> 24:05.610
He doesn't even attend the dinners,
so why?

24:10.323 --> 24:12.325
[mellow music playing]

24:16.204 --> 24:18.123
[Sa-eon] What's this?
It came out of nowhere.

24:24.671 --> 24:25.505
[sighs]

24:27.174 --> 24:28.675
[Hee-joo] Should I delete it now?

24:29.259 --> 24:30.552
That would be weirder.

24:31.428 --> 24:33.305
My stupid finger.

24:34.181 --> 24:35.182
[sighs]

24:36.224 --> 24:37.100
[chuckles softly]

24:39.519 --> 24:41.521
[Sa-eon] What does this mean?
Explain yourself.

24:44.774 --> 24:45.692
[sighs]

24:46.985 --> 24:47.986
"Explain yourself"?

24:48.069 --> 24:49.154
Is that too intense?

24:50.071 --> 24:50.989
[sighs]

24:52.199 --> 24:54.492
[mellow music continues playing]

24:57.078 --> 24:58.246
[phone thuds]

24:59.080 --> 24:59.998
[sighs softly]

25:00.081 --> 25:02.918
[Hee-joo] What do I do? I can't look.

25:09.466 --> 25:10.634
[Sa-eon] Congrats on passing.

25:25.357 --> 25:26.358
[music ends]

25:29.027 --> 25:29.986
[Sa-eon sighs]

25:33.615 --> 25:34.532
Mmm.

25:35.158 --> 25:37.661
It's good. Just how I like it. Great pick.

25:37.744 --> 25:39.329
I'm glad you enjoy it.

25:39.412 --> 25:40.580
[Young-woo chuckles]

25:40.664 --> 25:42.249
Try it, Mr. Paik.

25:42.958 --> 25:43.959
Okay.

25:47.837 --> 25:48.672
It's good.

25:48.755 --> 25:50.298
[both chuckling softly]

25:51.007 --> 25:52.926
- [phone vibrates]
- [employee] It is good.

25:55.971 --> 25:57.973
[Hee-joo] Thank you. It's thanks to you.

25:58.515 --> 25:59.349
[chuckles softly]

25:59.432 --> 26:01.434
[quirky music playing]

26:04.437 --> 26:05.438
[Sa-eon] No, it's not.

26:05.981 --> 26:08.316
Refrain from making statements
that could be misunderstood.

26:08.400 --> 26:11.319
Let me be clear.
There was no special treatment.

26:15.365 --> 26:16.658
[inhales sharply]

26:16.741 --> 26:18.535
Is it too stiff?

26:19.119 --> 26:21.162
It's fine for me. Mr. Paik!

26:22.205 --> 26:24.666
You must have weak teeth. [laughs]

26:29.087 --> 26:30.130
[phone vibrates]

26:32.966 --> 26:34.175
[Hee-joo] I'll buy you a meal.

26:34.259 --> 26:35.093
[scoffs]

26:36.386 --> 26:37.595
You'll buy me a meal?

26:42.142 --> 26:46.271
What's a good gift
to give someone who just got a job?

26:47.772 --> 26:49.816
- The latest cellphone.
- It's already the latest.

26:50.650 --> 26:52.110
A tablet? Laptop?

26:52.193 --> 26:53.069
They have both.

26:53.778 --> 26:54.612
What else?

26:54.696 --> 26:56.197
Share some ideas.

26:56.281 --> 26:57.615
Well, a wallet?

26:57.699 --> 26:59.784
- A bag?
- Not something you want.

26:59.868 --> 27:00.910
Something practical…

27:00.994 --> 27:03.330
- It doesn't have to be practical.
- …or not.

27:03.413 --> 27:05.123
- It doesn't have to be practical.
- Yeah.

27:05.206 --> 27:06.875
[Young-woo] Something sentimental.

27:06.958 --> 27:08.001
Something thoughtful.

27:08.585 --> 27:11.838
A new suit is pretty much
the go-to gift for a new job.

27:11.921 --> 27:13.256
Come on.

27:14.549 --> 27:15.550
A suit?

27:19.929 --> 27:21.014
Great pick.

27:21.097 --> 27:22.390
Yeah, not bad.

27:22.474 --> 27:24.184
[softly] A suit.

27:27.103 --> 27:28.646
[phone vibrates]

27:34.652 --> 27:36.654
[Sa-eon] Come here by six.

27:40.909 --> 27:42.911
[suspenseful music playing]

27:59.219 --> 28:01.471
[You-ri] You want to go in there?

28:02.639 --> 28:04.015
Yes.

28:05.683 --> 28:08.520
- [crow caws]
- [screams] Wait for me!

28:08.603 --> 28:09.687
[metal rattling]

28:10.605 --> 28:11.606
[You-ri] Goodness.

28:12.982 --> 28:15.026
- [metal rattling]
- No way.

28:15.110 --> 28:17.320
We can't go over this.

28:23.159 --> 28:24.160
What are you doing?

28:29.749 --> 28:31.000
[Sang-woo] I think it was here.

28:33.962 --> 28:34.796
What?

28:34.879 --> 28:36.297
A large portrait.

28:37.132 --> 28:39.259
I remember a huge hand with a dragon ring.

28:40.009 --> 28:40.844
[sighs]

28:42.679 --> 28:45.265
The room you played in every day.

28:45.932 --> 28:46.850
Where is it?

28:47.434 --> 28:48.601
That room.

28:49.477 --> 28:50.311
Follow me.

28:55.734 --> 28:57.360
[wind whistling]

29:08.830 --> 29:09.664
[You-ri] Wow.

29:12.792 --> 29:14.544
[inhales sharply] This is the room.

29:17.088 --> 29:18.590
I'm sure I saw it that day.

29:18.673 --> 29:20.008
What?

29:20.091 --> 29:21.259
A cute…

29:22.635 --> 29:23.845
cat.

29:23.928 --> 29:25.889
- [thunder rumbling]
- [rain pattering]

29:25.972 --> 29:27.515
[mysterious music playing]

29:27.599 --> 29:29.768
That child told me.

29:30.435 --> 29:31.644
"Want to play?"

29:32.937 --> 29:35.190
What? With what?

29:41.696 --> 29:43.364
Let's cut open the cat's belly.

29:47.660 --> 29:49.245
[Sang-woo] "Next, the tail."

29:51.039 --> 29:52.457
[thunder rumbling]

29:52.540 --> 29:53.833
"Next, the leg."

29:57.295 --> 29:58.463
"Next, the head."

30:00.340 --> 30:02.300
[mysterious music continues playing]

30:04.385 --> 30:05.845
[thunderclap]

30:10.517 --> 30:12.352
[young Sang-woo breathing heavily]

30:21.861 --> 30:22.821
[music fades]

30:22.904 --> 30:25.615
The way he spoke sounded so innocent.

30:25.698 --> 30:27.325
He said it as if it was nothing.

30:29.619 --> 30:30.870
It made it more terrifying.

30:36.376 --> 30:37.710
Missing?

30:39.003 --> 30:40.672
Yes, a few kids from the orphanage

30:40.755 --> 30:42.841
went missing shortly after being adopted.

30:42.924 --> 30:44.592
I learned that after becoming an adult.

30:46.511 --> 30:47.929
It's still an unsolved case.

30:49.597 --> 30:53.768
Do you remember what you said
at our first meeting?

30:54.644 --> 30:57.021
Instead of asking what it is,

30:57.105 --> 31:00.483
shouldn't you be asking
why I haven't revealed it yet?

31:00.567 --> 31:02.068
[suspenseful music playing]

31:02.151 --> 31:03.444
What's the reason?

31:03.528 --> 31:06.698
Why are you digging up something
that happened over 20 years ago?

31:07.824 --> 31:09.534
I was the first to discover that villa.

31:13.454 --> 31:15.456
I suggested to the kids that we go too.

31:16.374 --> 31:17.834
Once my channel grew big enough,

31:18.459 --> 31:21.546
I wanted to reveal it
when people started paying attention.

31:22.547 --> 31:25.508
Then I got the chance to be on the show
and thought, "This is it."

31:27.719 --> 31:30.138
You've been holding onto this
for a long time.

31:31.306 --> 31:32.557
I'm sorry.

31:35.059 --> 31:36.060
You are?

31:37.478 --> 31:38.646
For what?

31:39.230 --> 31:40.398
To be honest,

31:42.150 --> 31:47.196
Sa-eon asked me about you a few days ago.

31:47.280 --> 31:51.075
I told him you grew up in an orphanage
by mistake.

31:51.159 --> 31:53.912
Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon asked about me?

31:55.538 --> 31:56.456
Like what?

31:56.539 --> 31:59.125
You know, this and that.

32:01.461 --> 32:02.545
[phone vibrates]

32:05.757 --> 32:07.425
[gasps] Goodness!

32:07.508 --> 32:08.343
What is it?

32:08.426 --> 32:10.011
This is great for Hee-joo!

32:10.094 --> 32:11.262
What about Hee-joo?

32:12.347 --> 32:13.932
She's going to the presidential office.

32:19.604 --> 32:20.647
[elevator dings]

32:27.946 --> 32:29.530
Are you Ms. Hong Hee-joo?

32:30.657 --> 32:32.450
Right this way.

32:32.533 --> 32:34.577
Considering the professional setting,

32:34.661 --> 32:38.623
I went with a neutral and simple style
without any bold patterns or decorations.

32:38.706 --> 32:39.707
What do you think?

32:41.417 --> 32:43.836
The spokesperson's office called.

32:43.920 --> 32:47.298
He said that you're the sign language
interpreter for the presidential office.

32:47.382 --> 32:50.093
I was asked to prepare an outfit
suitable for you.

32:51.636 --> 32:53.304
Would you like to try it on?

32:58.434 --> 32:59.352
[elevator dings]

33:00.561 --> 33:01.646
[saleslady] Welcome.

33:03.523 --> 33:05.525
[intriguing music playing]

33:25.420 --> 33:26.546
[saleslady chuckles softly]

33:27.714 --> 33:29.966
It looks great with your complexion.

33:33.428 --> 33:37.348
But it looks a little big.
I'll get you one in a smaller size.

33:46.315 --> 33:48.609
You look so pretty.

33:49.360 --> 33:54.991
You have such great proportions.
That suit really flatters you. [chuckles]

33:55.700 --> 33:56.909
[Sa-eon] It looks good on you.

33:58.202 --> 33:59.078
We'll take it.

33:59.162 --> 34:01.039
Okay, I'll wrap it up.

34:01.122 --> 34:03.041
You can go ahead and change
if you're ready.

34:03.624 --> 34:05.418
[intriguing music continues playing]

34:09.797 --> 34:11.466
Try this one on too.

34:22.185 --> 34:23.978
[saleslady gasps, chuckles]

34:24.604 --> 34:26.189
[Sa-eon] Thank you. Goodbye.

34:26.272 --> 34:27.440
[manager] Take care.

34:39.202 --> 34:40.203
[music ends]

34:41.537 --> 34:43.206
Why didn't you try it on?

34:47.710 --> 34:49.462
[Hee-joo] I don't have to try it on
to know.

34:51.047 --> 34:51.881
Know what?

34:55.510 --> 34:57.595
I appreciate the suit. I'll wear it well.

34:57.678 --> 34:58.846
Let's go and eat now.

35:02.100 --> 35:03.059
[sighs]

35:04.769 --> 35:06.229
What do you know?

35:09.565 --> 35:12.068
I know something that flashy
doesn't really suit me.

35:12.151 --> 35:13.402
[Sa-eon sighs]

35:20.535 --> 35:23.371
I have nowhere to wear it to,
and it doesn't feel like it's for me.

35:23.454 --> 35:24.580
So why bother?

35:25.289 --> 35:26.916
Then, what about that?

35:31.212 --> 35:32.463
[soft music playing]

35:42.014 --> 35:43.141
[phone vibrating]

35:44.767 --> 35:47.812
PARK DO-JAE

35:48.688 --> 35:50.022
Yes, go ahead.

35:50.106 --> 35:52.525
The modulated voice analysis
isn't complete yet,

35:52.608 --> 35:54.610
but I just received a strange report.

35:55.194 --> 35:57.280
- What strange report?
- [Do-jae] Don't be surprised.

35:57.905 --> 36:00.867
Based on the waveform
and spectrogram analysis, 406 is…

36:00.950 --> 36:02.827
[suspenseful music playing]

36:10.459 --> 36:11.544
[Sa-eon] A woman?

36:12.461 --> 36:13.296
Are you sure?

36:13.379 --> 36:16.215
Of course, there's a possibility
of an accomplice,

36:16.299 --> 36:18.176
- or it could be a decoy.
- A decoy?

36:18.259 --> 36:21.304
Using someone else's voice
without being the perpetrator.

36:21.387 --> 36:23.556
You mean like a recording
or reading a script?

36:24.599 --> 36:25.892
It's definitely not that.

36:26.434 --> 36:29.979
The conversations weren't just
regurgitated on command like a parrot

36:30.062 --> 36:32.857
but were more like real-time exchanges.

36:32.940 --> 36:34.775
Rule out the possibility of recordings.

36:34.859 --> 36:37.653
- Proceed with the analysis…
- [door opens, closes]

36:49.540 --> 36:51.292
[pleasant music playing]

37:27.787 --> 37:28.621
Hong Hee-joo.

37:30.248 --> 37:33.793
Underestimating yourself is a bad habit.

37:35.169 --> 37:38.381
I'd like to help you break that bad habit.

37:39.590 --> 37:40.800
What do you think?

37:43.219 --> 37:45.346
[mellow music playing]

38:01.612 --> 38:02.697
It's expensive.

38:04.907 --> 38:06.158
It says it's Hanwoo.

38:10.830 --> 38:11.831
I want jjajangmyeon.

38:12.581 --> 38:13.749
That's enough.

38:22.008 --> 38:24.218
[sighs]

38:26.637 --> 38:28.014
With sweet and sour pork.

38:28.889 --> 38:29.807
[chuckles softly]

38:31.809 --> 38:32.727
SANG-WOO

38:33.769 --> 38:34.812
[quirky music playing]

38:34.895 --> 38:36.188
[phone vibrates]

38:36.647 --> 38:37.898
[phone vibrates]

38:37.982 --> 38:41.319
[Sang-woo] Hee-joo, I heard the news.
Congrats on the interpreter job.

38:47.199 --> 38:48.451
Do you want some wine?

38:48.534 --> 38:50.703
You-ri wants to congratulate you too.

38:54.248 --> 38:56.375
[Hee-joo] Sang-woo, I'm sorry,
but next time…

38:56.459 --> 38:57.501
Go now.

38:59.003 --> 39:01.088
But with me.

39:03.507 --> 39:04.508
[sighs]

39:05.593 --> 39:06.802
[bottle pops]

39:06.927 --> 39:09.180
- [You-ri] Congratulations, Hee-joo.
- [Sang-woo] Congrats.

39:17.897 --> 39:19.106
[glasses clinking]

39:23.402 --> 39:24.236
[exhales]

39:29.700 --> 39:31.452
But how did you two come together?

39:34.497 --> 39:36.248
She said she'd buy me dinner.

39:37.166 --> 39:38.334
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo.

39:38.417 --> 39:40.336
She did? Why?

39:41.087 --> 39:41.921
Can she not?

39:42.004 --> 39:43.589
[Sang-woo] Not without a reason.

39:43.672 --> 39:44.840
There must be one.

39:46.300 --> 39:47.676
Then why are you two together?

39:47.760 --> 39:49.428
We're coming back from covering a site.

39:50.137 --> 39:52.973
You know that we're doing a show together.

39:53.057 --> 39:55.768
- You-ri told me you asked her about me.
- [You-ri gasps]

39:57.395 --> 39:59.355
What's the story about?

39:59.438 --> 40:00.439
Oh…

40:01.190 --> 40:02.108
Well…

40:02.733 --> 40:05.945
A case of missing children
from an orphanage.

40:06.028 --> 40:08.322
[Sang-woo] We can't discuss it
due to program security.

40:08.406 --> 40:09.782
I'm sorry I cut you off.

40:09.865 --> 40:11.617
Will you answer me now?

40:11.700 --> 40:12.785
Tell me.

40:14.870 --> 40:16.872
Why are you so interested in me?

40:21.043 --> 40:22.628
[Hee-joo] Hey, Sang-woo.

40:23.421 --> 40:25.756
Didn't you want to congratulate me?

40:25.840 --> 40:26.674
Yeah.

40:29.593 --> 40:30.428
Sorry.

40:32.221 --> 40:35.850
Hee-joo, the sign language interpreter
for the presidential office.

40:37.226 --> 40:38.769
Yeah, it's something to congratulate,

40:39.395 --> 40:41.480
but wasn't your dream something else?

40:43.065 --> 40:44.275
[mellow music playing]

40:52.408 --> 40:54.076
LEAVE NEWSCASTER APPLICATION HERE

40:58.456 --> 40:59.874
NAME: HONG HEE-JOO

41:31.572 --> 41:33.240
[music ends]

41:36.202 --> 41:38.204
[upbeat song playing]

42:42.977 --> 42:44.395
[song playing over speakers]

42:55.823 --> 42:56.657
[song stops playing]

43:00.035 --> 43:01.412
[mellow music playing]

43:13.299 --> 43:16.427
[Sang-woo] After that, we listened
to music often in the broadcast room.

43:18.887 --> 43:19.888
Oh.

43:21.390 --> 43:24.143
Did something happen
between you two in college?

43:25.519 --> 43:27.855
Right? I can totally sense it.

43:27.938 --> 43:29.064
You have a bad sense.

43:29.648 --> 43:31.483
You're known for that.

43:31.567 --> 43:32.401
[scoffs]

43:33.193 --> 43:34.486
Me?

43:34.570 --> 43:36.989
What I said is based on facts.

43:37.072 --> 43:39.158
It's crystal clear.

43:39.241 --> 43:40.451
A college broadcast room

43:41.243 --> 43:43.662
is perfect for flirting. [giggles]

43:44.371 --> 43:45.789
[amusing music playing]

43:47.249 --> 43:48.125
[inhales]

43:50.711 --> 43:52.296
Did you two flirt?

43:53.297 --> 43:55.549
[You-ri] Why would you ask that?
They totally did!

43:55.633 --> 43:58.344
Why else would Hee-joo go
to the broadcast room?

43:58.427 --> 44:00.095
It wasn't to be a newscaster.

44:02.681 --> 44:03.849
[Sang-woo] She could be one.

44:05.392 --> 44:06.518
Can she not?

44:07.686 --> 44:08.520
Excuse me?

44:10.064 --> 44:13.859
But how could she be a newscaster?

44:18.739 --> 44:19.573
[chuckles nervously]

44:20.574 --> 44:23.243
Of course, she can. What I meant was…

44:23.911 --> 44:26.080
She could definitely be a newscaster.

44:26.163 --> 44:28.707
You must have dreamed
of becoming a newscaster.

44:29.500 --> 44:31.210
I didn't know. [chuckles nervously]

44:31.960 --> 44:34.046
Why are you bringing that up now?

44:34.129 --> 44:36.965
She's the sign language interpreter
for the presidential office.

44:38.133 --> 44:39.677
Why ask about her dream now?

44:41.929 --> 44:44.473
- Are you trying to rain on her parade?
- You think I am?

44:49.353 --> 44:50.979
She wants us to stop.

44:53.357 --> 44:55.609
"It's true I wanted to be a newscaster
in the past."

44:56.693 --> 45:00.155
"Now, I'm happy to be the sign language
interpreter for the presidential office."

45:03.283 --> 45:04.535
[Hee-joo] Got it?

45:13.836 --> 45:14.670
[door opens]

45:15.587 --> 45:17.047
[door closes]

45:18.549 --> 45:19.716
[drink pouring]

45:24.930 --> 45:25.806
[chuckles softly]

45:26.432 --> 45:27.516
It's just…

45:27.599 --> 45:30.185
My glass was empty. [chuckles]

45:32.855 --> 45:33.939
[phone vibrates]

45:36.275 --> 45:38.277
IN-A

45:38.360 --> 45:40.612
IT'S ME. HOW ARE YOU? IT'S BEEN A WHILE.

45:40.696 --> 45:42.114
[slow music playing]

45:47.035 --> 45:47.870
[You-ri] Hey.

45:49.037 --> 45:51.623
Do you think Hee-joo went to the bathroom?

45:52.833 --> 45:53.667
I'll go check.

45:54.251 --> 45:55.252
Who wants ice cream?

45:57.212 --> 45:58.046
All of a sudden?

45:58.714 --> 45:59.840
[You-ri] Me!

45:59.923 --> 46:00.841
I want chocolate!

46:02.676 --> 46:03.760
Get me whatever!

46:05.596 --> 46:06.680
[panting]

46:08.474 --> 46:09.308
Hey, sis!

46:10.017 --> 46:13.770
Something really fun
happened at school today.

46:13.854 --> 46:15.022
I'll tell you.

46:16.190 --> 46:19.318
A friend sent me a note.

46:21.612 --> 46:23.572
Do you know what was written on it?

46:24.156 --> 46:25.157
[doorbell rings]

46:25.991 --> 46:28.202
PAIK SA-EON

46:46.887 --> 46:47.846
Why are you here?

46:55.896 --> 46:59.024
[young Hee-joo] I'm going to pass on
what you say to my sister.

46:59.107 --> 46:59.942
You?

47:04.321 --> 47:05.572
I heard you're deaf.

47:06.156 --> 47:08.575
Why don't you wear hearing aids
or learn to sign?

47:12.287 --> 47:13.205
[sighs]

47:13.288 --> 47:14.831
[slow music playing]

47:19.002 --> 47:22.172
[young Hee-joo] He looks forward
to studying math with you!

47:26.051 --> 47:27.177
[young Sa-eon] Solve it.

47:46.572 --> 47:47.573
[sighs softly]

48:02.504 --> 48:03.547
Do it again.

48:04.298 --> 48:06.758
Another mistake
and I'll pour water on your head.

48:07.884 --> 48:09.553
[slow music continues playing]

48:12.639 --> 48:15.267
[young Hee-joo] In-a, solve it again.
You can do better.

48:26.278 --> 48:27.613
[phone vibrating]

48:33.410 --> 48:34.578
[Sa-eon] I'm glad you called.

48:34.661 --> 48:36.246
I had a question for you.

48:37.039 --> 48:38.540
[Hee-joo] A question for me?

48:39.708 --> 48:40.876
What is it?

48:40.959 --> 48:43.670
Have you heard Hee-joo's voice before?

48:48.759 --> 48:49.968
What are you saying?

48:50.052 --> 48:51.845
She can't speak. How could I?

48:52.471 --> 48:56.099
Then do you know why she can't speak?

48:56.725 --> 48:59.394
Since the accident that caused Hong In-a
to lose her hearing,

48:59.478 --> 49:00.812
she hasn't worn hearing aids.

49:00.896 --> 49:02.147
She didn't learn to sign.

49:02.814 --> 49:04.650
Instead, she took Hee-joo around

49:04.733 --> 49:06.777
and had her convey people's words
through notes.

49:06.860 --> 49:09.780
She lost her brother,
and her sister went deaf.

49:09.863 --> 49:13.116
How could she be okay after that?
She shouldn't be.

49:14.368 --> 49:16.244
[mysterious music playing]

49:16.328 --> 49:17.412
Wait.

49:18.413 --> 49:19.831
Is it because of Hong In-a?

49:20.666 --> 49:23.168
What do you mean?

49:23.251 --> 49:24.127
[scoffs]

49:25.754 --> 49:28.674
Chairman Hong's only biological daughter
became disabled,

49:29.549 --> 49:31.677
and Hee-joo,
who lived under the same roof…

49:33.845 --> 49:36.264
was probably forced to keep quiet too.

49:37.683 --> 49:39.768
That's the ridiculous story I had in mind.

49:41.812 --> 49:43.063
Aside from that,

49:43.980 --> 49:45.399
I can't find another reason.

49:45.982 --> 49:47.484
[Hee-joo] You've mentioned before

49:47.567 --> 49:50.362
that you have no intention
of letting Hong Hee-joo go.

49:51.363 --> 49:52.239
If Hong In-a returns,

49:53.824 --> 49:56.076
will you still feel the same?

49:58.203 --> 50:00.247
Yes, I will.

50:00.872 --> 50:03.083
Why? Why won't you let her go?

50:03.166 --> 50:05.210
- A sense of responsibility?
- No.

50:05.293 --> 50:06.211
Then…

50:08.171 --> 50:09.005
is it sympathy?

50:13.969 --> 50:15.721
What did you just say?

50:16.430 --> 50:17.472
Sympathy?

50:18.056 --> 50:20.392
I'll say it once,
so listen carefully, 406.

50:20.475 --> 50:21.810
My true feelings for Hee-joo…

50:21.893 --> 50:23.186
[car revving]

50:25.439 --> 50:26.440
Paik Sa-eon!

50:34.322 --> 50:35.449
[car revving]

50:39.995 --> 50:41.580
- [Hee-joo panting]
- [Sa-eon groans]

50:41.663 --> 50:43.582
[both breathing heavily]

50:43.665 --> 50:45.125
[slow music playing]

50:49.671 --> 50:50.672
[groans]

50:50.756 --> 50:51.923
[breathing heavily]

51:05.854 --> 51:07.522
You don't need to go to the hospital?

51:09.691 --> 51:10.525
[sighs]

51:11.735 --> 51:13.945
You work with your hands,
so you have to be careful.

51:14.029 --> 51:15.530
How many times have I told you?

51:16.740 --> 51:18.158
[sighs] Have you no fear?

51:18.909 --> 51:20.285
Where did you come from?

51:22.370 --> 51:23.705
And how are you so strong?

51:24.414 --> 51:25.665
You took me down.

51:30.170 --> 51:31.296
[Hee-joo] Paik Sa-eon!

51:31.379 --> 51:33.089
[intriguing music playing]

51:36.426 --> 51:37.260
I…

51:40.222 --> 51:41.306
think I heard it.

51:42.474 --> 51:43.475
Your voice.

51:47.229 --> 51:48.563
Did you call my name?

51:51.066 --> 51:52.275
I want to hear it again.

51:53.693 --> 51:54.611
Your voice.

51:57.155 --> 51:57.989
Hong Hee-joo.

51:58.573 --> 52:00.867
The world won't fall apart
if you speak up.

52:02.077 --> 52:03.161
Everything you want to say,

52:03.245 --> 52:04.830
the things you've held back…

52:06.540 --> 52:07.833
Say whatever you want.

52:23.348 --> 52:25.016
IT'S ME. HOW ARE YOU? IT'S BEEN A WHILE.

52:25.100 --> 52:26.977
[intriguing music continues playing]

52:55.589 --> 52:56.673
[Sa-eon] Hong Hee-joo.

52:57.257 --> 53:00.844
Underestimating yourself is a bad habit.

53:00.927 --> 53:04.764
I'd like to help you break that bad habit.

53:05.974 --> 53:07.058
What do you think?

53:14.149 --> 53:15.108
[phone vibrating]

53:20.238 --> 53:21.281
[phone vibrating]

53:22.991 --> 53:25.452
UNKNOWN CALLER

53:26.286 --> 53:27.287
[phone vibrating]

53:27.370 --> 53:28.997
[breathing heavily]

53:29.080 --> 53:31.374
[eerie music playing]

53:33.376 --> 53:34.878
[kidnapper] Sis!

53:34.961 --> 53:36.129
How have you been?

53:38.131 --> 53:40.216
Welcome and congratulations.

53:44.804 --> 53:45.680
What's your name?

53:45.764 --> 53:47.474
It's Jeong Won-bin.

53:47.557 --> 53:48.642
Won-bin.

53:48.725 --> 53:50.727
You live up to your name, don't you?

53:51.478 --> 53:53.897
The face-off for who's more handsome
will be intense.

53:53.980 --> 53:56.191
No way, I could never compete.

53:56.733 --> 53:59.861
- I hear we look alike though. [laughs]
- [press secretary laughs]

54:06.368 --> 54:07.243
What's your name?

54:09.621 --> 54:10.664
[chuckles]

54:10.747 --> 54:13.458
I'm sorry.
I don't know sign language. [laughs]

54:15.710 --> 54:16.544
I see.

54:17.671 --> 54:21.132
How can we communicate during work?

54:21.216 --> 54:23.259
Shall we all learn sign language?

54:25.261 --> 54:26.721
I'm thinking of learning it.

54:27.681 --> 54:28.515
You?

54:28.598 --> 54:29.432
Yes.

54:30.058 --> 54:33.770
That way, I can ensure the interpreters
are conveying my words accurately.

54:34.521 --> 54:36.398
If there's any difference in nuance,

54:36.481 --> 54:38.316
I'll be able to correct it.

54:38.400 --> 54:40.735
[Hee-joo] Sign language isn't difficult.

54:40.819 --> 54:44.739
If you learn it, there won't be issues
communicating with me either.

54:47.784 --> 54:50.120
I'm going to start learning it today.

54:50.745 --> 54:51.955
[press secretary] Wow.

54:52.038 --> 54:53.498
A spokesperson who can sign.

54:53.581 --> 54:58.086
Social media will eat that up.
Think of all the likes.

54:58.169 --> 54:59.921
- [all laughing]
- You're right.

55:00.005 --> 55:01.589
[all applauding]

55:01.673 --> 55:04.509
- [male assistant] Welcome.
- [press secretary] Congratulations.

55:06.636 --> 55:07.887
FINGER ALPHABET

55:09.597 --> 55:11.850
I've already memorized this.

55:17.147 --> 55:18.398
I've prepared in advance.

55:18.940 --> 55:20.150
It wasn't that hard.

55:22.819 --> 55:25.363
"A. B."

55:25.989 --> 55:27.907
"C. D."

55:41.796 --> 55:43.465
"A hundred questions, a hundred answers"?

55:44.049 --> 55:49.971
"Write down one word or sentence you want
to learn in sign language every day."

55:51.014 --> 55:52.432
Starting today?

55:55.143 --> 55:56.061
Hmm.

56:07.655 --> 56:08.865
Teach me.

56:17.123 --> 56:19.250
[soft song playing]

56:30.261 --> 56:31.096
What about this?

57:06.172 --> 57:07.549
[song continues playing]

57:22.272 --> 57:25.275
[Sa-eon] I look forward
to working with you.

57:29.988 --> 57:30.822
Hong.

57:33.658 --> 57:34.492
Hee.

57:37.078 --> 57:38.079
Joo.

57:39.330 --> 57:42.167
Interpreter.

57:47.380 --> 57:48.214
What?

57:48.923 --> 57:50.008
Did I get it wrong?

57:55.138 --> 57:58.266
[Hee-joo] I look forward
to working with you as well.

58:03.354 --> 58:07.025
Paik Sa-eon.

58:09.068 --> 58:10.487
Spokesperson.

58:13.907 --> 58:14.824
[scoffs]

58:23.041 --> 58:24.167
[Sa-eon chuckles softly]

58:26.503 --> 58:28.296
- [indistinct chatter]
- [sizzling]

58:36.763 --> 58:37.680
[patting]

58:49.984 --> 58:50.818
Excuse me?

58:51.653 --> 58:52.487
Sir?

58:53.530 --> 58:54.405
Yes?

58:54.948 --> 58:58.868
You don't usually come to team dinners,
so I just came to our usual spot.

58:58.952 --> 59:01.329
What do you think? Is it okay?

59:02.497 --> 59:04.666
Yes, it's fine.

59:04.749 --> 59:06.251
I'm relieved to hear it.

59:06.334 --> 59:08.378
There's no place better than this
for a team dinner.

59:08.461 --> 59:10.380
[all chuckling nervously]

59:10.463 --> 59:11.881
- [Sa-eon] Mr. Kang.
- Yes?

59:11.965 --> 59:13.633
What are you doing?

59:14.634 --> 59:16.302
Excuse me? I don't…

59:16.386 --> 59:18.388
The meat's burning.

59:18.471 --> 59:19.472
I see!

59:20.390 --> 59:21.307
I'll…

59:21.391 --> 59:22.600
[playful music playing]

59:23.226 --> 59:24.269
[Young-woo groans softly]

59:42.495 --> 59:44.497
- [male assistant] Wow.
- [Young-woo] Whoa!

59:44.581 --> 59:45.915
[camera shutter clicking]

59:45.999 --> 59:47.166
[exclaims]

59:48.710 --> 59:50.295
[all exclaim]

59:54.591 --> 59:55.425
Let's eat.

59:55.508 --> 59:57.176
- Yes, sir.
- [all] Thank you.

01:00:00.096 --> 01:00:01.139
[Young-woo clears throat]

01:00:02.098 --> 01:00:02.932
[Young-woo] What?

01:00:03.016 --> 01:00:04.225
[chuckles softly]

01:00:04.309 --> 01:00:06.519
You grilled it perfectly! It's delicious.

01:00:06.603 --> 01:00:08.688
[employee 1] It's really good.

01:00:10.273 --> 01:00:11.399
Eat up, everyone.

01:00:12.275 --> 01:00:13.109
[phone vibrating]

01:00:14.360 --> 01:00:16.321
- [Young-woo] Do you want some?
- [employee 2] Yes.

01:00:16.404 --> 01:00:17.655
[Young-woo] It's so good.

01:00:18.698 --> 01:00:19.991
- A big one.
- [employee 2] Thanks.

01:00:20.074 --> 01:00:21.784
- [assistant] Me too.
- We don't have enough.

01:00:25.330 --> 01:00:26.331
[Young-woo] Um,

01:00:27.081 --> 01:00:28.750
sir, should we…

01:00:29.792 --> 01:00:30.627
do a toast--

01:00:31.210 --> 01:00:32.170
[Young-woo whispering]

01:00:33.504 --> 01:00:34.881
[Sa-eon clears throat]

01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:43.264
[interpreter] What?

01:00:45.141 --> 01:00:47.310
We look forward
to working with you as well!

01:00:47.393 --> 01:00:48.770
That's what that means.

01:00:48.853 --> 01:00:49.854
- Goodness.
- I see.

01:00:49.937 --> 01:00:51.731
- Let's toast.
- Everyone, enjoy!

01:00:51.814 --> 01:00:52.982
- Enjoy!
- Cheers!

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:53.941
[Young-woo] Welcome!

01:00:54.651 --> 01:00:57.654
This is Mr. Paik's treat. It's on him.

01:00:57.737 --> 01:00:59.113
Help yourselves.

01:01:01.699 --> 01:01:02.825
[Young-woo exclaims]

01:01:03.993 --> 01:01:05.203
[Young-woo exhales]

01:01:05.286 --> 01:01:06.871
[employee 1] It's so good.

01:01:07.497 --> 01:01:08.998
[Do-jae] Sir, just a moment.

01:01:16.130 --> 01:01:18.800
- [Young-woo] Eat. Yes.
- [employee 1] Eat up. I need more alcohol.

01:01:18.883 --> 01:01:20.718
- [Young-woo] I'll pour it.
- [employee 1] Yeah.

01:01:21.636 --> 01:01:23.054
The call just came in.

01:01:23.137 --> 01:01:26.599
The voice analysis was almost complete,
but malware was detected.

01:01:26.683 --> 01:01:29.143
- The computer shut down completely.
- So what?

01:01:29.227 --> 01:01:30.937
Most of the original files are gone,

01:01:31.521 --> 01:01:34.399
but we were able to get results
from the recovered fragmented files.

01:01:34.982 --> 01:01:36.484
The audio quality isn't great.

01:01:36.567 --> 01:01:37.777
Can I listen to it?

01:01:37.860 --> 01:01:39.028
Yes, but…

01:01:40.279 --> 01:01:41.656
Please listen to it first.

01:01:44.283 --> 01:01:46.285
[suspenseful music playing]

01:02:03.052 --> 01:02:05.638
[kidnapper] Sis, are you okay?

01:02:05.722 --> 01:02:07.223
Were you hurt anywhere?

01:02:09.475 --> 01:02:10.643
You know, from earlier.

01:02:11.185 --> 01:02:13.146
You ran in front of a moving car.

01:02:15.189 --> 01:02:16.399
[car revving]

01:02:18.943 --> 01:02:20.778
[kidnapper laughing]

01:02:21.988 --> 01:02:24.532
You said you were getting a divorce.

01:02:24.615 --> 01:02:25.867
[laughing]

01:02:25.950 --> 01:02:28.119
So you changed your mind.

01:02:29.245 --> 01:02:30.872
You won't divorce him, will you?

01:02:32.790 --> 01:02:34.709
Why do you want me to divorce him?

01:02:35.543 --> 01:02:36.544
[kidnapper] Because…

01:02:37.670 --> 01:02:39.589
I want to see that bastard,

01:02:40.506 --> 01:02:42.008
Paik Sa-eon, be ruined.

01:02:42.717 --> 01:02:44.218
What about you, Sis?

01:02:44.302 --> 01:02:45.178
[sniffles]

01:02:46.095 --> 01:02:47.346
Do you know him well?

01:02:49.015 --> 01:02:50.349
No, I bet you don't.

01:02:51.309 --> 01:02:53.019
You probably don't know him at all.

01:02:54.437 --> 01:02:55.605
What do you know?

01:02:55.688 --> 01:02:57.440
How well do you know him?

01:02:57.523 --> 01:02:58.399
[kidnapper] Me?

01:02:58.983 --> 01:03:00.151
[scoffs]

01:03:00.234 --> 01:03:02.904
Why would you say something so hurtful?

01:03:05.198 --> 01:03:06.407
Listen carefully.

01:03:06.491 --> 01:03:08.201
In this world,

01:03:10.077 --> 01:03:13.164
the person who knows Paik Sa-eon
the best is me.

01:03:13.998 --> 01:03:16.334
Hurry, Sis. You're running out of time.

01:03:16.959 --> 01:03:19.378
Paik Sa-eon will find out soon.

01:03:21.088 --> 01:03:22.924
- What?
- [kidnapper] What do you think?

01:03:23.925 --> 01:03:25.802
Your true identity, Sis!

01:03:25.885 --> 01:03:27.887
[suspenseful music continues playing]

01:03:32.892 --> 01:03:35.311
[Sa-eon] Everything you want to say,
things you've held back…

01:03:36.938 --> 01:03:38.314
Say whatever you want.

01:03:44.695 --> 01:03:46.531
[Hee-joo] What I have to say to you…

01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:49.909
isn't what you want to hear.

01:03:52.787 --> 01:03:54.247
[over earphones] Decide by tomorrow.

01:03:54.330 --> 01:03:57.375
Or we can settle for two billion won.
You have until tomorrow.

01:04:01.879 --> 01:04:03.256
Can you guess who it is?

01:04:04.257 --> 01:04:06.050
Someone who's close to you

01:04:06.592 --> 01:04:07.927
and knows you--

01:04:08.010 --> 01:04:09.053
What's the age range?

01:04:09.136 --> 01:04:11.973
The waveform analysis indicates
a woman in her twenties.

01:04:23.860 --> 01:04:26.445
- [Young-woo] We don't do that here.
- [employee 1] No.

01:04:26.529 --> 01:04:29.615
- We don't pressure people to drink…
- That's right.

01:04:32.076 --> 01:04:35.204
[Sa-eon] So where did you get
your information on Hong Hee-joo?

01:04:35.788 --> 01:04:37.373
Are you close to me?

01:04:39.250 --> 01:04:41.878
[Do-jae] Don't be surprised.
The hotel you're at right now.

01:04:41.961 --> 01:04:43.796
[Hee-joo] Please, let me out!

01:04:43.880 --> 01:04:44.881
[scoffs]

01:04:46.799 --> 01:04:49.385
I'll send you another audio file.

01:04:49.468 --> 01:04:52.263
Analyze the sound waveform
and compare it with 406.

01:04:53.055 --> 01:04:55.391
See how much they match in percentage.

01:04:55.474 --> 01:04:57.018
Up to two decimal places.

01:04:58.185 --> 01:04:59.020
Yes, sir.

01:05:03.274 --> 01:05:05.276
[dramatic music playing]

01:05:07.695 --> 01:05:09.655
[employee 2] I wanted to do it.

01:05:12.366 --> 01:05:14.702
[indistinct chatter]

01:05:35.640 --> 01:05:37.558
Let's have one more round.

01:05:37.642 --> 01:05:39.268
- [employee 1] Come on.
- Wait. No.

01:05:39.352 --> 01:05:40.186
[Won-bin] Get in.

01:05:47.151 --> 01:05:47.985
[engine starting]

01:05:48.069 --> 01:05:49.862
[Young-woo] Thank you for the dinner!

01:05:49.946 --> 01:05:51.405
Have a good night.

01:05:51.489 --> 01:05:52.573
- Goodbye.
- Take care.

01:05:52.657 --> 01:05:53.991
[all] Goodbye.

01:05:55.534 --> 01:05:59.789
Wow, his first team dinner
and first time drunk.

01:06:00.831 --> 01:06:02.249
Is something going on?

01:06:02.333 --> 01:06:03.960
Mr. Park, do you know anything?

01:06:04.669 --> 01:06:05.878
No.

01:06:07.421 --> 01:06:10.508
Didn't you see them leave together?
I saw you two whispering.

01:06:10.591 --> 01:06:11.425
There's nothing.

01:06:13.219 --> 01:06:14.470
Let's go for another round.

01:06:14.553 --> 01:06:16.138
- No.
- [Young-woo] We're friends.

01:06:16.222 --> 01:06:17.807
- Let's go.
- [employee 2] Mr. Kang, wait!

01:06:17.890 --> 01:06:20.810
- [assistant] Let's go to karaoke! Karaoke!
- [employee 2] Let's go home.

01:06:25.648 --> 01:06:26.649
Sir?

01:06:27.733 --> 01:06:28.567
Sir?

01:06:30.361 --> 01:06:31.278
[Sa-eon sighs wearily]

01:06:33.155 --> 01:06:34.240
I'm fine.

01:06:34.323 --> 01:06:36.117
You may go.

01:06:36.200 --> 01:06:37.076
Yes, sir.

01:07:28.627 --> 01:07:29.503
[sighs]

01:07:42.475 --> 01:07:43.517
[thuds]

01:07:44.685 --> 01:07:47.229
- [phone vibrates]
- [Do-jae] I'm sorry to bother you so late.

01:07:47.313 --> 01:07:49.273
The analysis results came in.

01:07:49.356 --> 01:07:52.943
It's a 99.99% match.

01:08:09.627 --> 01:08:10.878
[soft song playing]

01:09:11.355 --> 01:09:14.275
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:09:14.817 --> 01:09:15.943
[Sa-eon groans]

01:09:16.026 --> 01:09:18.821
[Sa-eon] Tell me if something happened.

01:09:19.488 --> 01:09:21.866
[Hee-joo] Should I tell you
everything honestly?

01:09:21.949 --> 01:09:24.410
[Do-jae] You have an idea
who 406 might be, don't you?

01:09:24.493 --> 01:09:27.204
[Hee-joo] How about we each
ask a question and answer?

01:09:28.289 --> 01:09:30.666
[Sa-eon] By any chance, does Hee-joo want…

01:09:30.749 --> 01:09:31.917
sincerity

01:09:32.001 --> 01:09:32.918
and affection?

01:09:33.669 --> 01:09:35.087
Is that what she wants?

01:09:35.713 --> 01:09:37.131
I can give her everything.

01:09:38.007 --> 01:09:40.843
If that's what Hee-joo wants,
I'll give as much as she needs.

01:09:40.926 --> 01:09:42.303
Hong Hee-joo!

01:09:47.391 --> 01:09:49.393
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
